{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QLaplacianSpectralTower","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QLaplacianSpectralTower","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.qIntegerNumerator_vanishes_at_truncRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.qIntegerNumerator_vanishes_at_truncRoot","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-laplacian-spectral-tower.lean#L56-L66","doc":"**Root-of-unity truncation.** The unnormalised q-integer numerator\n`q^r − q^{−r}` vanishes at `q = ζ_r = exp(iπ/r)`. Since\n`ζ_r ^ r = −1` and `ζ_r ^ {−r} = (−1)^{−1} = −1`, the numerator is\n`(−1) − (−1) = 0`. This is the level-`r` Verlinde / WRT truncation that\ncollapses the infinite q-Laplacian spectrum to a finite, exact set. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-laplacian-spectral-tower","label":"prop:q-laplacian-spectral-tower","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-laplacian-spectral-tower.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.truncRoot_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.truncRoot_pow","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-laplacian-spectral-tower.lean#L45-L54","doc":"`ζ_r ^ r = −1` (so `ζ_r ^ (2r) = 1`): the r-th power of the\ntruncation root is `exp(iπ) = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.truncRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.truncRoot","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-laplacian-spectral-tower.lean#L41-L43","doc":"The primitive root of unity `ζ_r = exp(iπ/r)` at which the\nrepresentation category truncates at level `r`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}